A user gave me some feedback that if you copy the create-instant-app command manually, the $ will come with it. 

Made it so the $ is select-none. 

@nezaj @dwwoelfel @drew-harris

It's only a dev dependency, but MCP Inspector has had a min node version of 22.7.5 [for a bit](https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/inspector/pull/318). If you try to install using a Node version less than that, you'll get a warning.

Fixes #132 

```
npm warn EBADENGINE Unsupported engine {
npm warn EBADENGINE   package: '@modelcontextprotocol/inspector@0.16.6',
npm warn EBADENGINE   required: { node: '>=22.7.5' },
npm warn EBADENGINE   current: { node: 'v20.19.0', npm: '11.3.0' }
npm warn EBADENGINE }
```
